  "id": "reorganization-principle",
  "term": "reorganization principle",
  "definition": "The reorganization principle refers to the way the brain’s network arrangement changes with aging rather than simply declining overall. In this study, it described a shift in metabolic brain connectivity, with reduced strong hub-to-hub connections and increased feeder and local connections.",
